Z||000002||MrPBody||01-18-2001||08:23 PM||||That's more or less the process, but you'll probably do it lying on your back in the rain with rust and crud falling in your eyes, and barely enough room to use a hacksaw.<P>When you reassemble it, squeeze the pipes inward with pry bars and/or blocks to tension the mounting springs as you tighten the clamps.<P>If you want to replace the cat, Rodney Dickman sells a replacement.  (Cat Kit?)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||01-18-2001||09:41 PM||||check your local autoparts store for an exhaust pipe cutter.  looks lke a chain type thing that you wrap around the pipe.  makes it so much easier than a hacksaw. i know autozone has them for 25 bucks and you return it when your done.  loan a tool program they have.  good luck<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">       <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"<BR><A HREF="http://expage.com/kissmyssfiero" TARGET=_blank>KissMySSFiero.mywebsite.hehe</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||01-19-2001||10:32 PM||||MrP,  (Cat Kit?) <BR> No...try a "KitCat"  He He.<BR>Sorry...its that English humour...||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||01-19-2001||10:42 PM||||The whole process is so much easier if you just remove the complete exhaust system.  It really simple to remove the whole system. 10-15 minutes if headpipes loosen.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||01-20-2001||10:25 AM||||Exhaust work is a lot easier if you are friends with a mechanic who will let you use a lift.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Motorhead||01-20-2001||03:15 PM||||My car is "CAT"less. And it has benefitted from the operation.  If you have a smog inspection the alternative is to gut the existing cat and leave it in place.  Went through a tailpipe test and passed with a gutted cat.  The car ran great!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000008||Greg Piet||01-20-2001||03:24 PM||||Skitime...<BR>I dunno where you got 10-15 minutes...<BR>It takes me at least 5-10 minutes to get my ebrake equalizer off so I can remove the exhaust.  then another 5-10 to put it back on.  It always seems to eat up a minimum of 45 minutes to swap exhaust systems, but then again I also have to remove my rear swaybar as well.<BR><P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
Z||000009||kinboyatuwo||01-20-2001||04:40 PM||||Thanks for all the help, i will probibly be doing this with it on jackstands and with a lot of rust in the eye.<P>i found a place here to get a performance cat but i think i will just get rid of it<P>cant gut it it has a whole or that would work<P>chris<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||4
Z||000010||skitime||01-20-2001||06:06 PM||||Greg Piet why would you even have to touch the E-brake.  Remove two head pipe bolts, two screws holding the four rear springs at the back of the cradle then I remove the four front springs and finally remove the hanger clamps on each tailpipe. The sway bar doesn't need to be touched either.  I have an 88 so maybe things are a lot easier on them.<p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 01-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Greg Piet||01-20-2001||09:24 PM||||My muffler and muffler output pipes are blocked by the e brake equalizer and cables.  I tried to wiggle it out and no dice.   hmmmmm now im confused.<P>As far as the swaybar goes there is about 1/2 inch clearance between the exhaust pipe  and the swaybar (the swaybar even has a bend in it to allow the exhaust pipe to clear it).  I cannot see how it is possible to wiggle the entire exhaust system  out with that little crearance.<P>Where o where is a Fiero owner who has an 88 and pre 88 V6 to clarify.||||reg||1
Z||000012||skitime||01-20-2001||10:32 PM||||Greg, I guess I am lucky with the 88 this time. Neither the E-brake or sway bar are anywhere near the exhaust.  It all drops cleanly in one piece. Clean and simple. Usually the 88s are the one with extra grief.<p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 01-20-2001).]||||reg||1
